From: ceamkrier <ceamkrier@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 04:25:25 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] fix: keep the text of every line a table run's span
 covers

The region classifier skips every line inside a table run's span, so text
the table leaves out of its cells is dropped from the markdown. A run that
binned only some columns of its rows, or a sparse run stretched over a
column of worked solutions, lost whole lines that the text output keeps:
a spec sheet's capacity rows and model numbers, a page of exam answers,
the footnotes under a parts table.

Two guards, on every run the classifier emits:

- A pipe-table run whose cells and interstitials carry under 70% of the
  non-space characters of its span is read as text instead. Across 1,333
  runs on three corpora, every run that left out whole lines sat below
  0.7 and every benchmark table kept 0.73 or more.
- In a run that stays, a line no cell took a single word from is handed
  back as an interstitial, so it is emitted ahead of the table. A line
  sharing any word with the table stays with it, so nothing is repeated.
